    {
      "post_id": 37480,
      "author_username": "boarderlib",
      "author_user_id": 793,
      "timestamp_iso": "2018-05-31T14:28:30+00:00",
      "timestamp_epoch_ms": 1527776910000,
      "timestamp_raw": "May 31, 2018 9:28:30 GMT -5",
      "body_html": "First pitcher May 5th, and as of yesterday this is what I have. Boy what a difference 25 days can make. <br/><img src=\"https://uploads.tapatalk-cdn.com/20180531/df5f6b920f5d19811d75a797b56a69a3.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/>Leucophylla 'purple lips' first spring pitcher.  The looks are there, but I have to wait until fall for the size. <br/><img src=\"https://uploads.tapatalk-cdn.com/20180531/62a1b2f7af61c97a66431a36ffdc0b49.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/>I get googly eyed every time I look at this hybrid. flava var cuprea BH x rubricorpora UCD select solid 'red'<br/><img src=\"https://uploads.tapatalk-cdn.com/20180531/32968414be99a01c0c7e272a5ed72f4d.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><img src=\"https://uploads.tapatalk-cdn.com/20180531/b8e19a16b9725e23b28c81c5e49d05a9.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/>A slight change in appearance from its first picture posted earlier this month. Oreophila being photo bombed by an imposter 'abandoned hope' and one of my favorite ornata's. <img src=\"https://uploads.tapatalk-cdn.com/20180531/7f7598dbffd347e659785aad209f2172.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/>",
